      en: ["The Gulf of Guinea covers an area of approximately 2.35 million km².", "It is where the Prime Meridian and the Equator intersect (Null Island).", "Nigeria's coastline along the gulf stretches for about 853 kilometers.", "The gulf contains some of the world's largest untapped deep-water oil reserves.", "It is a major transit point for nearly 25% of Africa's total maritime trade.", "The warm Guinea Current maintains water temperatures above 25°C year-round."],
